From 32a4d5462fdfd9da5f06a69018a3325ee67b45d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.local>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 12:01:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Build NIN Modification as a manually-processed service (6
 request types)

Techhub has no API for NIN Modification yet (confirmed against
techhubltd.co/nin_modifications.php), so unlike every other identity
service, nothing is called automatically at submit time. Instead:

- Customer picks one of 6 modification types (Update Name, Phone, DOB,
  Address, Name & DOB, Name & Phone), each with its own price (matching
  techhubltd.co's own listed prices) and its own field set matching their
  form exactly, including the full parentage/demographic block DOB changes
  require.
- Wallet is debited immediately (PIN-confirmed, same requirePinConfirmation
  boundary as every other purchase route).
- A PDF of exactly what was submitted is generated server-side and sealed
  (encrypted) alongside the form data - the same document an admin opens to
  manually re-key the request on techhubltd.co.
- Transaction stays PENDING until an admin either marks it complete (new
  'Complete modification' AdminJS action, SUPPORT-blocked) or rejects it
  (existing 'reverse' action, extended to allow this one case from PENDING
  - it already refunds correctly).
- New SUPER_ADMIN-only, audit-logged PDF download route at
  /admin/nin-modification/:id/pdf.
- Web: new dedicated /nin-modification page, tile-arranged the same way as
  the rest of the NIN Services hub. AppShell's NIN Services submenu was
  already simplified upstream to a single 'All NIN Services' link, so no
  sidebar change was needed here.

Known scope limits, flagged for follow-up:
- State/LGA fields are plain text, not a Nigeria states+LGAs dropdown
  dataset.
- Flutter parity not yet built - web only in this patch.
- Supporting-document upload is accepted as base64 in the sealed PII blob
  but is not embedded into the generated PDF; an admin retrieves it via the
  existing 'View PII' action, not the PDF download.
